From d24ad829a7b5d4ca1336c07726560fe123be746f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:05:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add experimental 3-a-side match mode (route-A prototype)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Small-sided prototype: each team fields GK + 2 outfielders. The 8 surplus
outfielders per team are ghosted at pitch entry using the existing red-card
machinery (sentAway=1, cards=-1, parked at the sent-off spot), so every
system that already excludes sent-off players — control election, pass
targets, set-piece takers, break repositioning, wall math, the Mode3
arrival wait — handles them unmodified.

Port-side holes patched, each gated on SmallSided.Enabled so 11-a-side
behaviour and the RNG stream stay byte-identical when off:
- UpdatePlayers: in-play tactical repositioning had no sentAway gate
  (the asm only checks it on the stoppage path)
- UpdatePlayers: the port-only controlled-player re-election stand-in
  could elect a parked ghost
- Main: the renderer painted all 22 slots unconditionally
- Bench: substitutions are gated off in 3v3 (bench slots would unghost)

New 'mode' slot on the match-setup screen toggles 11v11 / 3v3.
See docs/3v3-PROTOTYPE.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
