+# 3-a-side prototype (experimental)
+
+**Status:** route-A prototype (2026-08-04). One human + 5 AI players on a
+full-size pitch: each team fields its goalkeeper + 2 outfielders (ordinals
+2 and 3 — tactics rows 0 and 1 of the selected formation).
+
+## How it works
+
+Instead of resizing the 11-per-team engine, the 8 surplus outfielders per
+team are marked exactly like red-carded players (`sentAway = 1`,
+`cards = -1`) and parked off-pitch at match start
+(`Kickoff.InitPlayersBeforeEnteringPitch`). Every engine system that already
+excludes sent-off players — controlled-player election, pass-target
+election, set-piece taker scans, break repositioning, the free-kick wall
+math, the Mode3 arrival wait — then does the right thing unmodified. See
+`game/scripts/Sim/Port/SmallSided.cs` for the full list and the four
+port-side holes that needed explicit patches (in-play repositioning, the
+re-election stand-in, the renderer, the bench).
+
+With the mode **off** (the default), behaviour — including the RNG stream
+and the recorded golden traces — is byte-identical to 11-a-side.
+
+## How to try it
+
+1. Set up OpenSWOS normally (see the root `README.md`: Godot 4 + .NET, plus
+   your own SWOS 96/97 Amiga `.adf` files in `original_swos_adf/`).
+2. Start the game. On the match-setup screen, move focus down to the new
+   **`mode`** slot and press left/right to switch `11 v 11` → `3 v 3
+   (experimental)`.
+3. `opponent : AI`, then space to kick off. You control the nearest player
+   (classic SWOS switching) — GK + 2 outfielders — against a 3-man CPU team.
+4. The toggle is read at match start; flipping it mid-match does nothing
+   until the next match.
+
+## Known limitations (accepted for the prototype)
+
+- Full-size pitch — 3v3 feels sparse; a smaller pitch is a much bigger job.
+- No substitutions in 3v3 (the bench is gated off).
+- Restart formations use tactics rows 0-1, so the two outfielders line up
+  like a right back + right centre back; purpose-built 3v3 position tables
+  are route-B work.
+- When defending a free kick, both outfielders join the wall (the original
+  wall takes ordinals 2-5).
+- Penalty shootouts are untested in this mode.
